     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Planning to use ggvis/rCharts etc as well, I just need to keep all avenues open, as there&#39;ll always be ggplots generated by our R users. </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, 24 July 2015 17:38:40 UTC+1, Andrew Clancy  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all, <div><br></div><div>Can shiny output ggplots as svg easily, rather than png? </div><div>I&#39;m using the interactive ggplot features, so <a href=\"https://github.com/timelyportfolio/svgPanZoom\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/timelyportfolio/svgPanZoom&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397498496000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oJCM-HB6Xvlph33Rv8PuS\">svgPanZoom</a> doesnt help (but is cool, and could also be useful). </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
